# API & RAML Design Standards

## API-Led Connectivity
- Follow the three-tier API-led architecture:
  - **Experience APIs** (`exp`): consumer-facing, orchestration
  - **Process APIs** (`proc`): business logic, composition
  - **System APIs** (`sys`): backend system integration
- Each API should serve a single tier — do not mix layers

## RAML Project Naming
- **No regional prefix** — Do NOT add regional prefixes (e.g., `na-`, `eu-`, `apac-`) per leadership directive
- Pattern: `{name}-{layer}-api-spec`
  - **{name}**: Logical application name (e.g., `sfl-leads`, `drupal`, `benefits-investigation`)
  - **{layer}**: API layer — `sys` (system), `proc` (process), or `exp` (experience)
- Lower case, hyphen-separated
- Root RAML file name must match the project name (e.g., `sfl-leads-sys-api-spec.raml`)

## RAML File & Folder Conventions
- Folder names: **camelCase** (e.g., `dataTypes`, `enumTypes`, `traits`, `examples`)
- All non-root files: **TitleCase** (e.g., `OrdersDataType.raml`, `ErrorResponsesTrait.raml`)
- **Examples folder** (`examples/*.raml`): Use TitleCase for example files (e.g., `LeadRequestExample.raml`, `LeadResponseExample.raml`). Do not use lowercase-hyphenated names (e.g., `lead-request-example.raml`).
- Library imports: use **TitleCase** names (e.g., `ProduceTypes`, `GlobalResponses`)

## RESTful Resource Design
- Top-level resources represent business domain nouns (e.g., `/employees`, `/orders`)
- Collections use **plural** names (e.g., `/accounts`)
- Singular resources use **singular** names (e.g., `/account/{id}`)
- Verbs as sub-resources are only acceptable in Experience/Process APIs for triggering processes

## API URL Pattern
- Base path: `/{project-name}/api/{version}/`
- Example: `/sfl-leads-sys-api/api/v1/`
- Version in URL matches the major semantic version (`v1`, `v2`, etc.)
- Use a fixed `baseUri` when a single host applies; avoid redundant `baseUriParameters` with only one default value

## Anypoint Exchange
- When published to Exchange, update the asset title to user-friendly Title Case
- Example: `sfl-leads-sys-api-spec` → "SFL Leads System API"

## RAML Resource Type Placement
- Apply `type` (resource type) to **resources** only — not to methods. RAML 1.0 does not support `type` on operation nodes.

## Review Checklist
- [ ] RAML project follows `{name}-{layer}-api-spec` naming (no regional prefix)
- [ ] Resource types applied at resource level (not under get/post)
- [ ] Folder names are camelCase, non-root files are TitleCase
- [ ] Example files in `examples/` use TitleCase (e.g., `LeadRequestExample.raml`)
- [ ] Resources are nouns representing domain entities
- [ ] Collections use plural naming
- [ ] API URL follows `/{project}/api/{version}/` pattern
